        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1375">

                <pb facs="1071" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/909.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Mr. Parker,
                        representing American interests in Mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department encloses a copy of a
                    despatch [of November 5] from the Vice Consul at Guadalajara, Mexico, setting
                    forth the arbitrary manner in which mining interests are being treated by the
                    present de facto government in Mexico.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to bring the statements contained therein to the attention of
                    the appropriate authorities, in connection with previous representations, and
                    earnestly to continue your efforts for a material modification of the decree
                    imposing increased taxes upon mining properties.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
